        <groundspeak:log id="691246530">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-06-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="265062">nicolo</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP591 - Elnora

N 52° 03.351 W 113° 17.450&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;{FOUND}&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Six weeks after my DNF ( or DNGT, Did Not Get There ) we were back on this road after checking out the Three Hills Cruise Weekend with two of our grandkiddies ... no tornadoes today ;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This time we took a south approach, with my wife driving. The road was really OK but was damp in some spots, with gravel spread on dicey spots. In spite of this, Karen was a little shaken up and I took over the driving after about 1 km. We made fairly quick progress to the cap area and I hopped out. Hot day, lots of bugs. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I spotted what I thought was the marker post and headed right to it ... NOTHING! I used van der Decken's photo for guidance but nothing, nothing but long grass. That's when I noticed that I was 10 meters from the cap ... DOH, another marker post!!! After that it was a quick location of the depression and somewhat successful work exposing the cap for a photo ... not very well as I had nothing to move the dirt out of the cap depression.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anywho, great area, beautiful views from up here. I really enjoyed the drive up to the cap : narrow, dirt road, tons of green and &quot;lakes&quot; all over the place.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
